The firmament, as described in Genesis  1:6-8, is commonly interpreted in Christian teaching as the expanse of the heavens that serves as a boundary between the earthly and divine realms. This symbolism highlights God's creative power and the ordered structure of the universe, where the firmament acts as a divider between the waters above and below.

